## cfl_variant_create

```c
struct cfl_variant *cfl_variant_create()
{
    struct cfl_variant *instance;

    instance = calloc(1, sizeof(struct cfl_variant));
    if (instance == NULL) {
        cfl_errno();
        return NULL;
    }
    instance->size = 0;

    return instance;
}
```

## cfl_variant_destroy

```c
void cfl_variant_destroy(struct cfl_variant *instance)
{
    if (!instance) {
        return;
    }

    cfl_container_release_variant(instance);

    if (instance->type == CFL_VARIANT_STRING ||
        instance->type == CFL_VARIANT_BYTES) {
        if (instance->data.as_string != NULL && !instance->referenced) {
            cfl_sds_destroy(instance->data.as_string);
        }
    }
    else if (instance->type == CFL_VARIANT_ARRAY) {
        cfl_array_destroy(instance->data.as_array);
    }
    else if (instance->type == CFL_VARIANT_KVLIST) {
        cfl_kvlist_destroy(instance->data.as_kvlist);
    }

    free(instance);
}
```

## Notes on `referenced` handling and size assignment

- **Referenced parameter**: In both the string and bytes creators, the flag is normalized via `instance->referenced = referenced ? CFL_TRUE : CFL_FALSE;`. When set, the pointer is stored directly (no copy). Otherwise, a copy is made using `cfl_sds_create_len`.

- **Destroy interaction**: In `cfl_variant_destroy`, an SDS string/bytes buffer is freed only if it is non-NULL and *not* referenced — a referenced pointer is left untouched (the caller owns it).

- **Size field assignments**:
  - `cfl_variant_create` initializes `instance->size = 0;`
  - The string and bytes creators call `cfl_variant_size_set(instance, value_size)` and `cfl_variant_size_set(instance, length)` respectively, which internally sets `var->size = size;`.

